                <note rend="inline" type="source">Paris Peace Conf.184.015/104a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Commission to Negotiate
                            Peace to the Chief of the Mission to the Baltic Provinces</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Greene</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-08-04">August 4, 1919</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>87. From Tyler: Baltic Commission recalled Colonel Greene and personnel to
                    proceed to Paris to report to Ammission, after winding up affairs of
                    Commission.</p>
                <closer><hi rendition="#small-caps">Am</hi>[<hi rendition="#small-caps">erican</hi>]
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mission</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
